Compile as C99 on QNX: its C headers are not C89

opusfile compiles with -std=c89 -pedantic. QNX's C library headers are C99
-- stdlib.h declares atexit() "static inline" -- and do not compile as C89
("expected ';' before 'int'"). On QNX add -std=gnu99 after it (the last -std
wins); the warnings it asks for stay.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -46,6 +46,11 @@
 
 # Platform-specific tweaks
 case $host in
+  *-nto-qnx*)
+    # QNX's C library headers use C99 (static inline): -std=c89 cannot
+    #  compile them. The later -std wins.
+    CC_CHECK_CFLAGS_APPEND([-std=gnu99])
+    ;;
   *-mingw*)
     # -std=c89 causes some warnings under mingw.
     CC_CHECK_CFLAGS_APPEND([-U__STRICT_ANSI__])
